.TH ptx 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
ptx \- produce a permuted index of file contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY ptx
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ INPUT \~.\|.\|.\&]
\~#\~(without -G)
.YS
.SY ptx
.B \-G
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ INPUT
.RI [ OUTPUT ]]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Output a permuted index, including context, of the words in the input files.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-A
\fB\-A, \-\-auto\-reference\fP
.UE
output automatically generated references
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-G
\fB\-G, \-\-traditional\fP
.UE
behave more like System V 'ptx'
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-F
\fB\-F, \-\-flag\-truncation=\,STRING\fP
.UE
use STRING for flagging line truncations.
The default is '/'
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-M
\fB\-M, \-\-macro\-name=\,STRING\fP
.UE
macro name to use instead of 'xx'
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-O
\fB\-O, \-\-format=\,roff\fP
.UE
generate output as roff directives
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-R
\fB\-R, \-\-right\-side\-refs\fP
.UE
put references at right, not counted in \fB\-w\fR
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-S
\fB\-S, \-\-sentence\-regexp=\,REGEXP\fP
.UE
for end of lines or end of sentences
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-T
\fB\-T, \-\-format=\,tex\fP
.UE
generate output as TeX directives
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-W
\fB\-W, \-\-word\-regexp=\,REGEXP\fP
.UE
use REGEXP to match each keyword
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-b
\fB\-b, \-\-break\-file=\,FILE\fP
.UE
word break characters in this FILE
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-f
\fB\-f, \-\-ignore\-case\fP
.UE
fold lower case to upper case for sorting
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-g
\fB\-g, \-\-gap\-size=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
gap size in columns between output fields
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-i
\fB\-i, \-\-ignore\-file=\,FILE\fP
.UE
read ignore word list from FILE
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-o
\fB\-o, \-\-only\-file=\,FILE\fP
.UE
read only word list from this FILE
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-r
\fB\-r, \-\-references\fP
.UE
first field of each line is a reference
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-t
\fB\-t, \-\-typeset\-mode\fP
.UE
change the default width from 72 to 100
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#ptx\-w
\fB\-w, \-\-width=\,NUMBER\fP
.UE
output width in columns, reference excluded
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/ptx#ptx\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/ptx#ptx\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
